WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.214 line:91%
Chapter 2. Connect the students' phones.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:10.994 line:91%
Students answer on their phones, in the web browser. There is no app to install, and no account.

00:00:11.458 --> 00:00:19.333 line:91%
Your phone and the students' phones must be on the same Wi-Fi, or on your phone's hotspot. You do not need the internet.

00:00:20.504 --> 00:00:23.653 line:91%
In the menu, open "Connect phones".

00:00:24.979 --> 00:00:29.114 line:91%
Students scan this QR code with the camera of their phone.

00:00:29.573 --> 00:00:32.454 line:91%
Or they type this address in the browser.

00:00:32.919 --> 00:00:38.774 line:91%
Make the QR code bigger, or show it full screen, so students at the back can scan it.

00:00:39.227 --> 00:00:42.013 line:91%
Tap anywhere to close the full screen.

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:49.154 line:91%
The phone opens MI WAY. It waits here. When you start a test, it appears on the phone by itself.

00:00:49.608 --> 00:00:56.874 line:91%
Android students can also install their own app: MI WAY Student. Press "Install the app on a phone".

00:00:58.048 --> 00:01:05.686 line:91%
Students scan this second QR code and tap "Download the app". It comes from your phone, so they don't need the internet.

00:01:06.145 --> 00:01:18.746 line:91%
The first time, the student taps your name. After that, the app finds your phone by itself, on any Wi-Fi, and joins with their own name. iPhones keep using the QR code in Safari.

00:01:19.918 --> 00:01:26.406 line:91%
The first time, test with your own phone. If the page does not open, follow this check list.

00:01:26.872 --> 00:01:36.426 line:91%
Many school Wi-Fi networks block phones. Then turn on your phone's hotspot: press "Open hotspot settings". Mobile data can stay off.

00:01:36.887 --> 00:01:47.066 line:91%
Most phones allow only about 10 phones on their hotspot. For a full class, students work in pairs, or you use a small pocket Wi-Fi router.

00:01:47.529 --> 00:01:57.126 line:91%
Using a hotspot? Type its name and password here once. Students scan this Wi-Fi QR code to join it without typing the password.
